<title>NEW ZEALAND: CBD New Zealand debuts at issue price.</title>
<headline>CBD New Zealand debuts at issue price.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property investment company CBD New Zealand debuted on the stock exchange on Tuesday at its issue price of NZ$1.</p>
<p>The company did not trade until early afternoon when a line of 4,000 shares was traded at $1 each.</p>
<p>The company's initial public offering closed on Friday with a minimum 19.5 million shares issued. The company had been seeking to raise between $19.5 million and $29.5 million.  </p>
<p>The company has said it intends targeting central business district buildings worth $10 million-$30 million because it believes that is where the growing strength is in the office market.</p>
<p>It owns one commercial office building in Auckland and has conditional contracts to buy two other buildings in the city.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
